{"id": "unknown-2026-06-03-012", "date": "2026-06-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Grid expansion, batteries to ease curtailment in Brazil", "content": "<p>Analysis by Aurora Energy Research indicates curtailment in Brazil could drop by 8 to 12 percentage points by the end of the decade, down from 21% in 2025.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/03/melhorias-na-rede-eletrica-e-entrada-de-baterias-no-medio-prazo-aliviarao-curtailment-projeta-aurora/\">Grid expansion, batteries to ease curtailment in Brazil</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/03/melhorias-na-rede-eletrica-e-entrada-de-baterias-no-medio-prazo-aliviarao-curtailment-projeta-aurora/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-03-013", "date": "2026-06-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Natural ester fluids beat mineral oil for use in renewable energy applications", "content": "<p>Compared with mineral oil, natural ester fluid enables the design of more compact, lighter, and thermally efficient transformers, helping photovoltaic applications reduce footprint, installation complexity, and overall project CAPEX compared with conventional mineral oil solutions.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/03/natural-ester-fluids-beat-mineral-oil-for-use-in-renewable-energy-applications/\">Natural ester fluids beat mineral oil for use in renewable energy app", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/03/natural-ester-fluids-beat-mineral-oil-for-use-in-renewable-energy-applications/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-03-014", "date": "2026-06-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.75, "keywords": ["record", "increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "France, Germany, Portugal, Spain set daily solar records", "content": "<p>Latest analysis from AleaSoft Energy Forecasting finds the weekly average electricity price increased in France, Portugal and Spain last week despite new daily solar records as wind energy production fell and demand increased.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/03/france-germany-portugal-spain-set-daily-solar-records/\">France, Germany, Portugal, Spain set daily solar records</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/03/france-germany-portugal-spain-set-daily-solar-records/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-03-015", "date": "2026-06-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Scientists achieve 27% efficiency in a co-deposited inverted perovskite", "content": "<p>Scientists in China have developed a new technique to prevent self-assembled molecules from clumping together and degrading co-deposited inverted perovskite cells. The approach enabled the highest certified power conversion efficiency reported for the architecture. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/03/scientists-achieve-27-efficiency-in-a-co-deposited-inverted-perovskite/\">Scientists achieve 27% efficiency in a co-deposited inverted perovskite</a> appeared first on", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/03/scientists-achieve-27-efficiency-in-a-co-deposited-inverted-perovskite/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "enphase-2026-06-03-016", "date": "2026-06-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["enphase"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Enphase explains how gallium nitride is changing its microinverters", "content": "<p><b>pv magazine</b> has spoken with Enphase chief product officer Raghu Belur about how gallium nitride technology is reshaping the company’s microinverter architecture. He highlighted gains in efficiency, power density and cost through its use of GaN-based bi-directional switch devices.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/03/enphase-explains-how-gallium-nitride-is-changing-its-microinverters/\">Enphase explains how gallium nitride is changing its microinverters</a> app", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/03/enphase-explains-how-gallium-nitride-is-changing-its-microinverters/", "type": "rss"}]}
